# A web shop handles four personal data breaches. Under Article 33 of the
# GDPR it notifies the supervisory authority within 72 hours of becoming
# aware of a breach, unless the breach is unlikely to result in a risk; under
# Article 34 it also tells the people affected when the risk is high, unless
# the data was encrypted (Article 34(3)(a)). Its hosting processor must alert
# it within 24 hours, a duty of their processing agreement, an ODRL agreement.
# The program finds that the lost laptop, the leaked customer database and
# the ransomware attack go to the authority, the database late; that only
# the database leak's 1200 customers must be told, the encrypted laptop being
# exempt; that the misdirected email is only documented; and that the
# processor broke its 24-hour duty for the database leak.
# Shows Logical English with namespace prefixes for ODRL 2.2 and DPV 2.3 with
# its personal data, risk and GDPR extensions: arithmetic over hours,
# comparisons, absence tests, an ODRL duty read by rules, and a sum.
# The risk levels are the controller's assessments, given as input.
# Sources https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/oj (Articles 28, 33, 34)
#         https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/
#         https://w3id.org/dpv/2.3/risk/ and https://w3id.org/dpv/legal/eu/gdpr

Use prefix ex with namespace "https://example.org/breach-notification#".
Use prefix odrl with namespace "http://www.w3.org/ns/odrl/2/".
Use prefix dpv with namespace "https://w3id.org/dpv#".
Use prefix pd with namespace "https://w3id.org/dpv/pd#".
Use prefix risk with namespace "https://w3id.org/dpv/risk#".
Use prefix gdpr with namespace "https://w3id.org/dpv/legal/eu/gdpr#".

# The processing agreement: the host may use the customer data, and must
# inform the shop of a breach within 24 hours.

ex:agreement is an odrl:Agreement and ex:agreement has odrl:assigner ex:webShop.
ex:agreement has odrl:permission ex:hosting.
ex:hosting is an odrl:Permission and ex:hosting has odrl:assignee ex:cloudHost.
ex:hosting has odrl:action odrl:use and ex:hosting has odrl:target ex:customerData.
ex:hosting has odrl:duty ex:alertShop.
ex:alertShop is an odrl:Duty and ex:alertShop has odrl:action odrl:inform.
ex:alertShop has odrl:constraint ex:within24Hours.
ex:within24Hours has odrl:leftOperand odrl:elapsedTime and ex:within24Hours has odrl:operator odrl:lteq.
ex:within24Hours has odrl:rightOperand 24.

# The breaches, with the shop's risk assessment. Hours count from the
# moment the shop became aware of each breach.

ex:lostLaptop is a risk:DataBreach and ex:lostLaptop has dpv:hasRisk risk:HighRisk.
ex:lostLaptop has dpv:hasPersonalData pd:Name and ex:lostLaptop has dpv:hasPersonalData pd:EmailAddress.
ex:lostLaptop has dpv:hasTechnicalMeasure dpv:Encryption and ex:lostLaptop has ex:affected 300.
ex:lostLaptop has ex:authorityNotifiedAt 40.

ex:databaseLeak is a risk:DataBreach and ex:databaseLeak has dpv:hasRisk risk:HighRisk.
ex:databaseLeak has dpv:hasPersonalData pd:MedicalHealth and ex:databaseLeak has ex:affected 1200.
ex:databaseLeak has ex:atProcessor ex:cloudHost and ex:databaseLeak has ex:processorAlertedAfter 30.
ex:databaseLeak has ex:authorityNotifiedAt 90.

ex:ransomware is a risk:DataBreach and ex:ransomware has dpv:hasRisk risk:ModerateRisk.
ex:ransomware has dpv:hasPersonalData pd:PurchasesAndSpendingHabit and ex:ransomware has ex:affected 5000.
ex:ransomware has ex:atProcessor ex:cloudHost and ex:ransomware has ex:processorAlertedAfter 6.
ex:ransomware has ex:authorityNotifiedAt 48.

ex:misdirectedEmail is a risk:DataBreach and ex:misdirectedEmail has dpv:hasRisk risk:LowRisk.
ex:misdirectedEmail has dpv:hasPersonalData pd:Name and ex:misdirectedEmail has ex:affected 1.

# Article 33(1): notify the authority unless the breach is unlikely to
# result in a risk, which the assessment expresses as low risk.

For every B,
if B is a risk:DataBreach and it is not known that B has dpv:hasRisk risk:LowRisk
then B has ex:requires gdpr:DPABreachNotice.
For every B, if B is a risk:DataBreach and B has dpv:hasRisk risk:LowRisk then B has ex:outcome ex:documentOnly.

# The 72-hour deadline, met or missed. A late notice must give reasons.

For every B and N,
if B has ex:requires gdpr:DPABreachNotice and B has ex:authorityNotifiedAt N and N is at most 72
then B has ex:authorityNotice ex:onTime.
For every B and N,
if B has ex:requires gdpr:DPABreachNotice and B has ex:authorityNotifiedAt N and N is greater than 72
then B has ex:authorityNotice ex:lateWithReasons.

# Article 34: tell the people affected of a high risk, unless the data was
# encrypted.

For every B,
if B has dpv:hasRisk risk:HighRisk and it is not known that B has dpv:hasTechnicalMeasure dpv:Encryption
then B has ex:requires gdpr:DataSubjectBreachNotice.
For every B,
if B has dpv:hasRisk risk:HighRisk and B has dpv:hasTechnicalMeasure dpv:Encryption
then B has ex:exemptFrom gdpr:DataSubjectBreachNotice.

# The processor's duty, read from the agreement: an inform duty limited by
# elapsed time, broken when the alert came later than the limit.

For every B and P and R and D and C and L and H,
if B has ex:atProcessor P and ex:agreement has odrl:permission R and R has odrl:assignee P and
R has odrl:duty D and D has odrl:action odrl:inform and D has odrl:constraint C and
C has odrl:leftOperand odrl:elapsedTime and C has odrl:operator odrl:lteq and C has odrl:rightOperand L and
B has ex:processorAlertedAfter H and H is greater than L
then B has ex:brokenDuty D.

# How many people must be told in all.

For every N,
if N is the sum of A for every B and A such that (B has ex:requires gdpr:DataSubjectBreachNotice and B has ex:affected A)
then ex:register has ex:peopleToInform N.

Find every B and D such that B has ex:requires D.
Find every B and S such that B has ex:authorityNotice S.
Find every B and D such that B has ex:exemptFrom D.
Find every B and O such that B has ex:outcome O.
Find every B and D such that B has ex:brokenDuty D.
Find every N such that ex:register has ex:peopleToInform N.
